Q1.layered architecture (or MVC + Service + Repository pattern)

“When a user sends a request, it first hits the entry point (index.js), then goes through the router to the controller. The controller delegates the request to the service layer, which contains business logic. The service calls the repository layer to interact with the database.
Once the database returns the data, it flows back through the repository, service, and controller, and finally the response is sent to the client.”

