What is React DOM?
👉 React DOM is a library that helps React show content on the web page (browser DOM)
📌 Simple:
👉 React → creates UI
👉 React DOM → displays UI in browser
1. Angular DOM
👉 Angular uses Real DOM
How it works:
•	When data changes → Angular updates full DOM tree 
•	Even small change → bigger update 
📌 Result:
•	Slower compared to React (for large apps) 
________________________________________
🔶 2. React DOM
👉 React uses Virtual DOM
How it works:
•	Creates a copy of DOM (Virtual DOM) 
•	Compares old vs new (diffing) 
•	Updates only changed part 
📌 Result:
•	Faster performance ✅ 



